  "outcome": "bounded-helper-fix-and-documentation-clarification-required; existing-three-model-Godot-evidence-supported",
  "summary": "The recorded church, mosque and Kailasa Godot audits are hash-bound actual runtime imports with unchanged expected triangle counts and 14 passing gates each. No rendering or game-performance result is established. The reusable Blender helper confuses mesh-declaration totals with scene-instance totals; the current seven models do not trigger it. The three quantized pyramid derivatives are outside the Godot preflight POSITION format and must be explicitly identified as unaudited.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "E3-R2-01",
      "severity": "medium",
      "status": "fix-required",
      "finding": "Blender comparison uses different counting bases for source and imported geometry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "integrations/heritage-assets/blender-review.py",
          "observation": "Source totals sum all meshes/primitives once, without traversing the active scene; imported totals sum each Blender mesh object in the scene."
        },
        {
          "path": "integrations/godot-heritage-review/test/fixture.mjs",
          "observation": "An actual fresh Blender 4.3.2 run of triangleGlb({instances:2}) produced sourceTriangles=1, importedTriangles=2, triangleCountDifference=1, sourceVertexEntries=3 and importedVertexEntries=6. The two instances are correct; no extra triangle was created by import.",
          "fixtureSha256": "c8a4bf2571fcecfee61b257eb237b7603aa75a3b34504dbbe6bcc183d3849b28"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A correct instanced input appears to change topology; an unused mesh can cause the reverse false discrepancy. A reused/unused mesh declaration must not be mistaken for a face-removal event. All seven current published models have each declared mesh referenced exactly once by the active scene, so their existing count comparisons are unaffected.",
